From 9b384b67f8b630f2b313a7d55d445cb05202fbfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:48:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(geometry): fit block curves after their INSERT
 placement

A SPLINE or ELLIPSE in a block was fitted in block units before the
placement, and the placement scaled the fit error without a change of
the stated bound. The block body now keeps the curve definition. Each
placed copy maps it exactly (ellipse centre and axes, spline control
points) and fits it in world units within CURVE_TOLERANCE_MM.

The similarity shortcut to an exact circle now needs an exact matrix.
A near similarity takes the ellipse path, which bounds the deviation
in drawing units, or refuses the curve by name.

Pinned by tests/dxf/block_curves.rs (review of PR #4052).

Refs #1865

